IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bnra-types`
IMPORT `bnra-part2-register`

-- Tests for Part 2, ss 25 to 31.  Thresholds read off the text: at least 30 days to object
-- (s 27(2)(b)).

§ `Tests -- Part 2, ss 25 to 31`

§§ `25. Rectification by General Division of High Court`

-- Court Rectification Facts: evidence adduced, a particular appears erroneous or defective, order requires a fresh document.
#ASSERT `the General Division of the High Court may direct the Registrar to rectify the register` (`Court Rectification Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the General Division of the High Court may direct the Registrar to rectify the register` (`Court Rectification Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the General Division of the High Court may direct the Registrar to rectify the register` (`Court Rectification Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar must rectify the register accordingly` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must rectify the register accordingly` FALSE
#ASSERT `the applicant must file a fresh document with a copy of the order and of the application` (`Court Rectification Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the applicant must file a fresh document with a copy of the order and of the application` (`Court Rectification Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)

§§ `26. Rectification by Registrar on application`

-- Rectification Notice Facts: lodged by the registered person or representative, error in a document of
-- particulars, typographical or clerical, error in filing, unintended and not prejudicial, would expunge a document.
`a typographical error in particulars` MEANS `Rectification Notice Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a substantive error in particulars` MEANS `Rectification Notice Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an unintended, harmless filing error` MEANS `Rectification Notice Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a filing error that prejudices someone` MEANS `Rectification Notice Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a typographical error notified by a stranger` MEANS `Rectification Notice Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a typographical error that could only be fixed by expunging a document` MEANS `Rectification Notice Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the Registrar may rectify the register on the notice` `a typographical error in particulars`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may rectify the register on the notice` `a substantive error in particulars`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may rectify the register on the notice` `an unintended, harmless filing error`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may rectify the register on the notice` `a filing error that prejudices someone`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may rectify the register on the notice` `a typographical error notified by a stranger`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may rectify the register on the notice` `a typographical error that could only be fixed by expunging a document`

§§ `27. Rectification or updating on Registrar's initiative`

-- Registrar Initiative Facts: satisfied of a grammatical or typographical defect, evidence of a conflict, written notice
-- not required in the circumstances, written notice given, days allowed to object, an objection was delivered,
-- objection frivolous, vexatious or withdrawn.
`a typographical defect, notice giving 30 days, no objection` MEANS `Registrar Initiative Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  30, FALSE, FALSE
`a typographical defect, notice giving 29 days` MEANS `Registrar Initiative Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  29, FALSE, FALSE
`a conflict in particulars, notice giving 30 days, no objection` MEANS `Registrar Initiative Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  30, FALSE, FALSE
`no defect and no conflict` MEANS `Registrar Initiative Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  30, FALSE, FALSE
`a defect, no notice given` MEANS `Registrar Initiative Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 0,  FALSE, FALSE
`a defect, no notice needed in the circumstances` MEANS `Registrar Initiative Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, 0,  FALSE, FALSE
`a defect, a genuine objection` MEANS `Registrar Initiative Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  30, TRUE,  FALSE
`a defect, a frivolous objection` MEANS `Registrar Initiative Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  30, TRUE,  TRUE

#ASSERT `the Registrar may rectify or update the register under section 27` `a typographical defect, notice giving 30 days, no objection`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may rectify or update the register under section 27` `a typographical defect, notice giving 29 days`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may rectify or update the register under section 27` `a conflict in particulars, notice giving 30 days, no objection`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may rectify or update the register under section 27` `no defect and no conflict`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may rectify or update the register under section 27` `a defect, no notice given`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may rectify or update the register under section 27` `a defect, no notice needed in the circumstances`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may rectify or update the register under section 27` `a defect, a genuine objection`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may rectify or update the register under section 27` `a defect, a frivolous objection`
#ASSERT `an objection stops the Registrar from rectifying or updating` `a defect, a genuine objection`
#ASSERT NOT `an objection stops the Registrar from rectifying or updating` `a defect, a frivolous objection`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may request the registered person to take steps to rectify the error or defect` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may request the registered person to take steps to rectify the error or defect` FALSE

§§ `28. Request for copy of notice of registration, etc.`

-- Copy Facts: fees paid, document destroyed under s 38, excluded document, electronic form after the 2024
-- commencement, entry is a notification means or date of birth or other prescribed information, entry is a
-- residential address, certified by the Registrar.
`a copy request with fees paid` MEANS `Copy Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a copy request without fees` MEANS `Copy Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a copy of a destroyed document` MEANS `Copy Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a copy of an excluded document` MEANS `Copy Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a certified copy` MEANS `Copy Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a date of birth in an electronic form` MEANS `Copy Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a date of birth in an older paper form` MEANS `Copy Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a residential address in an electronic form` MEANS `Copy Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`a residential address in an older paper form` MEANS `Copy Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE

#ASSERT `the person may require a copy or extract to be given or certified` `a copy request with fees paid`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may require a copy or extract to be given or certified` `a copy request without fees`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may require a copy or extract to be given or certified` `a copy of a destroyed document`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may require a copy or extract to be given or certified` `a copy of an excluded document`
#ASSERT `the certified copy or extract is admissible in evidence as of equal validity with the original` `a certified copy`
#ASSERT NOT `the certified copy or extract is admissible in evidence as of equal validity with the original` `a copy request with fees paid`
#ASSERT `the entry is excluded from the reference to a document in section 28(1)` `a date of birth in an electronic form`
#ASSERT NOT `the entry is excluded from the reference to a document in section 28(1)` `a date of birth in an older paper form`
#ASSERT `the Registrar must exclude the residential address from every copy or extract` `a residential address in an electronic form`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must exclude the residential address from every copy or extract` `a residential address in an older paper form`

§§ `29. Electronic transaction system`

#ASSERT `the Registrar may cause the system and the register to reflect the earlier date and time` (`Earlier Time Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cause the system and the register to reflect the earlier date and time` (`Earlier Time Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar must keep a record of the alteration` (`Earlier Time Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must keep a record of the alteration` (`Earlier Time Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `30. Transitional provision for contact address`

-- Contact Address Transition Facts: maintained an alternate address, the alternate address, residential address,
-- a change notice lodged after commencement, the contact address lodged.
#ASSERT `the individual's contact address for the purposes of the Act` (`Contact Address Transition Facts` OF TRUE,  "1 Alternate Road", "2 Home Street", FALSE, "") EQUALS "1 Alternate Road"
#ASSERT `the individual's contact address for the purposes of the Act` (`Contact Address Transition Facts` OF FALSE, "",                "2 Home Street", FALSE, "") EQUALS "2 Home Street"
#ASSERT `the individual's contact address for the purposes of the Act` (`Contact Address Transition Facts` OF TRUE,  "1 Alternate Road", "2 Home Street", TRUE,  "3 New Lane") EQUALS "3 New Lane"
#ASSERT `the individual's contact address for the purposes of the Act` (`Contact Address Transition Facts` OF FALSE, "",                "2 Home Street", TRUE,  "3 New Lane") EQUALS "3 New Lane"
#ASSERT `the transitional contact address is deemed a particular registered for the purposes of section 20(1)`

§§ `31. Disability of persons in default`

-- Disability Facts: required to be registered, contract made when (a) not registered, (b) cancelled and not restored,
-- (b) ceased and not restored, (c) in breach of ss 19(1) or 20(1) or (3); registration later restored; applied for relief;
-- default accidental; just and equitable; another party has sued; the defaulter counterclaims or sets off.
`a contract made while unregistered` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made after cancellation` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made after cessation` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made after cancellation, registration later restored` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made after cessation, registration later restored` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made in breach of section 19 or 20` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made while unregistered, though registered later` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made while properly registered` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a person not required to register` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made while unregistered, the other party sued and the defaulter counterclaims` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`a contract made while unregistered, the other party sued but the defaulter sues on its own claim` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`a contract made while unregistered, relief sought for inadvertence` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made while unregistered, relief sought as just and equitable` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made while unregistered, relief sought without a ground` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a contract made while unregistered, inadvertent, but no application` MEANS `Disability Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a contract made while unregistered`
#ASSERT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a contract made after cancellation`
#ASSERT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a contract made after cessation`
#ASSERT NOT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a contract made after cancellation, registration later restored`
#ASSERT NOT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a contract made after cessation, registration later restored`
#ASSERT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a contract made in breach of section 19 or 20`
-- s 31(3) lifts only the cancelled-or-ceased disability
#ASSERT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a contract made while unregistered, though registered later`
#ASSERT NOT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a contract made while properly registered`
#ASSERT NOT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a person not required to register`
#ASSERT NOT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a contract made while unregistered, the other party sued and the defaulter counterclaims`
#ASSERT `the defaulter may not enforce the right` `a contract made while unregistered, the other party sued but the defaulter sues on its own claim`
#ASSERT `the court may grant relief against the disability` `a contract made while unregistered, relief sought for inadvertence`
#ASSERT `the court may grant relief against the disability` `a contract made while unregistered, relief sought as just and equitable`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may grant relief against the disability` `a contract made while unregistered, relief sought without a ground`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may grant relief against the disability` `a contract made while unregistered, inadvertent, but no application`
#ASSERT NOT `section 31 affects the rights of any other party against the defaulter in respect of the contract`
